v 3
d phdid: Partial homogeneity in staggered difference-in-differences
d
d  Estimation, specification testing and diagnostics for staggered
d  difference-in-differences designs in which the cohort-time average
d  treatment effects are partially homogeneous -- equal within groups of
d  cohort-time cells, but not across them.  Implements the two estimators
d  of Arora and Wagle (2026): a Dirichlet process mixture fitted by
d  collapsed Gibbs sampling, and an l0-penalised partial-homogeneity
d  estimator with a two-step agglomerative search.  Includes tests for
d  recoverable heterogeneity, regularisation paths for both estimators,
d  exact partition enumeration, and sampler diagnostics.
d
d  Requires: Stata 17
d
d  Distribution-Date: 20261028
d
d Authors: Rohan Wagle and Parush Arora, Ashoka University
d Maintainer: Rohan Wagle
d Support: email rohan.wagle_ug2023@ashoka.edu.in
d
